{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: lane E, the clients. Build the HTTPS client library, the artroom CLI and the MCP server against the approved contract, so an agent needs only an MCP URL and git, and a person or script needs one command.","body":{"conditions":"(1) A client package implementing the contract's HttpRoom over the HTTPS routes and subscription (long poll and WebSocket), with Ed25519 envelope signing (RFC 8785 canonical bytes, idempotency keys), invitation redemption (client-custody join and the room-custody MCP redemption per R-ADM-12), workspaceToken retrieval only for the holder, Refusal values vs ArtroomError, and resumable cursors. (2) The npx artroom CLI: login/redeem, claim, workspace (prints the remote and configures git credentials without echoing the token), propose, note, review, land with wait, renew, release, attention, explain, log; plain text by default and --json; refusals print rule, reason and fix with a distinct exit code. (3) An MCP server (Agents SDK stateless MCP handler on Workers, plus a stdio mode for local agents) exposing exactly the contract's ten tools with their wire shapes, where each tool's description tells an agent what to do next on refusal. (4) A generated AGENTS.md block that teaches an agent the loop in under 30 lines. (5) Tests against a fake Room implementing the HTTPS routes (no live deploy needed): signing and canonical bytes vectors, idempotent retry, refusal handling, lost-response redemption with no leaked bearer and no silently consumed invitation, token never in logs or output, cursor resume; CLI snapshot tests; MCP tool schema tests. README in plain English per ISO 24495-1.","target_head":"53e7a3ecd97717598e48f60b8c42083dfeba24cc","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}